    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d493">

                <pb facs="0860" n="846" xml:id="pg846"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Boutwell, Secretary of the Treasury, to Mr. Rumley,
                        collector.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Treasury Department</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1869-10-07"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi>
                        7, 1869</date>.</dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">D. Rumley</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wilmington, North Carolina:</hi></p>
                <p>War Department has issued orders to Army officers at the fort to assist you.
                    Bring the Hornet under guns of fort. Take such possession of her, and, if
                    necessary, so far dismantle her as to make it impossible for her to go to sea,
                    until you have orders to release her.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. S. BOUTWELL,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of
                            Treasury.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
